rently 40.0)"],"break_rules":[{"id":"revenue_growth","label":"TTM revenue growth","metric":"revenue_growth","op":"<","threshold":0.07,"current":0.12},{"id":"roic","label":"ROIC","metric":"roic","op":"<","threshold":0.5413,"current":0.7218},{"id":"margin","label":"Operating margin change YoY","metric":"operating_margin_change","op":"<","threshold":-0.02,"current":0.06030929296545934},{"id":"rotation","label":"Consumer Discretionary rotation score","metric":"sector_rotation","op":"<","threshold":-30,"consecutive_weeks":2,"current":-69.0},{"id":"regime","label":"P(Stagflation)+P(Contraction)","metric":"adverse_regime_prob","op":">","threshold":55,"current":51.2},{"id":"trend","label":"Distance from 200dma","metric":"dist_200dma","op":"<","threshold":-10,"and_negative_rs":true,"current":-0.3},{"id":"theme","label":"Travel & Experiences theme trend","metric":"theme_trend","theme_id":"travel-experiences","op":"<","threshold":30,"current":40.0}],"narrative_note":"Narrative from the last 7 morning briefs' theme signals (exposure-weighted).","llm_enriched":true,"theme_exposures":[{"theme_id":"travel-experiences","theme":"Travel & Experiences","weight":0.5,"order":1,"effective":0.5}],"llm":{"thesis":"Expedia is compounding faster than its valuation implies: TTM revenue growth accelerated to 12% with margins up ~600bps and FCF up 123%, yet the stock trades at a 14.8% FCF yield and a P/E at the 0th percentile of its own 5-year history. The 22-point expectations gap (reality 63 vs pricing 41) suggests the market has not re-rated the improving operating leverage, likely because Consumer Discretionary is the second-worst rotating sector (-84) and near-term price action is weak (down 17% in a month, below 20/50-day averages). A strong balance sheet (net cash), aggressive buybacks (-5.4% dilution), and improving ROIC support a quality-at-a-discount setup, but sector flows and momentum are actively working against a re-rating catalyst in the near term. This is a fundamentals-ahead-of-price situation where patience and a sector-rotation shift are likely required to close the gap.","fundamental_read":"Revenue growth is accelerating (12.0% TTM vs 10.0% prior), operating margin expanded 603bps YoY to ~16%, and FCF grew 123% to a 28% margin, producing a reported ROIC above 70% (though incremental ROIC is unmeasured, tempering confidence in marginal returns). The balance sheet is net-cash (net debt/EBITDA -0.5), interest coverage is solid at 7x, and management is shrinking the share count (-5.4% dilution) while funding buybacks of ~$1.9B, indicating confident capital allocation.","technical_read":"Price sits just above the 200-day average (close 263 vs 260 SMA) but below both the 20-day (279) and 50-day (298) averages, reflecting a short-term downtrend within a longer-term uptrend (50>200). RSI at 36 and negative MACD histogram confirm weakening near-term momentum, with the stock 22% off its 52-week high despite a positive 12-month return of 19%.","market_expectation":"The combination of a rock-bottom P/E (0th percentile), EV/Sales at the 39th percentile, and a PEG of 0.15 implies the market is pricing in stagnant or deteriorating fundamentals rather than paying up for the current double-digit revenue acceleration and margin expansion \u2014 essentially a 'prove it' valuation despite already-visible operating improvement.","what_market_misses":["Reality score (63) materially exceeds pricing score (41), a 22-point gap that historically signals unrewarded fundamental improvement.","Revenue acceleration (+2pts sequentially) and margin expansion (+603bps) are occurring simultaneously, a combination the current multiple does not reflect.","Shareholder-friendly capital allocation (buybacks shrinking share count, net-cash balance sheet) is not being credited in a near-0th-percentile P/E."],"catalysts":["Next quarterly earnings report (~90 days post the 2026-08-06 filing) could confirm continued margin/revenue acceleration and force re-rating.","A shift in sector rotation sentiment toward Consumer Discretionary (currently -84, among the weakest) would remove a key technical headwind.","Continued buyback execution reducing share count could mechanically boost EPS growth already running near 98% YoY."],"risks":["Consumer Discretionary sector rotation is deeply negative (-84) and has persisted, which can keep the stock de-rated regardless of fundamentals.","Short-term technical deterioration (RSI 36, negative MACD, price below 20/50-day averages) suggests further near-term downside risk before any re-rating.","Macro regime is split nearly evenly across four scenarios (27.7% Goldilocks, 27.6% Contraction), leaving meaningful probability of an adverse backdrop for a travel-demand-sensitive business.","No engine-flagged estimate revisions or management guidance data are available, limiting confidence in forward consensus direction."],"thesis_break_conditions":["TTM revenue growth falls below 7% (from current 12.0%)","ROIC falls below 54% (from current 72.2%)","Operating margin YoY change turns negative beyond -2.0pts (from current +6.0pts)","Consumer Discretionary rotation score stays below -30 for two consecutive weeks (currently -84)","Adverse regime (Stagflation + Contraction) probability exceeds 55% (currently 49.9% combined)","Price closes >10% below its 200-day average with negative relative strength"],"second_order_beneficiaries":["Online travel infrastructure and payments providers (e.g., payment processors, cloud/booking-tech vendors) that benefit from Expedia's platform volume growth.","Hotel and short-term rental partners who gain distribution reach as Expedia's revenue and bookings scale.","Buyback counterparties and bondholders benefiting from a de-levered, cash-generative balance sheet that supports continued capital returns."],"epistemic_labels":[{"statement":"TTM revenue growth is 12.0% vs 10.0% prior quarter","kind":"observed_fact"},{"statement":"FCF grew 123.3% with a 28.4% FCF margin","kind":"observed_fact